      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195367/assets/f6b58865cc7048560bc547ed03b95977d5f9ed013cb411991a82d7da140717f7.png)\n\nFind the area of the triangle $△ABC.$\n\n(Figure not drawn to scale)",
      "worked_solution": "The area of the triangle is defined as \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n where $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding height.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the base is \n\n$$\nb=AC=5\n$$\n\nand the corresponding height is\n\n$$\nh=BC=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{b\\cdot h}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 8}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{2} \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
