    "q-87802": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87802",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195367/assets/3756b00cce29aad77b7a0b1ebb09f43cb89a602f8462edce89e8ba6346cb7fab.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Since $m∠A=m∠B$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AC=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {10}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 100 \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
