    "q-87801": {
      "dom_id": "step-q87801",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14195367/assets/f18be4b42008423fe08b165fea4b3807b247813112b92a6ad0932c07a33ba8b6.png)\n\nWhat is the area of the right triangle $ABC$ shown above?",
      "worked_solution": "Since $m∠A=m∠C$, we have an isosceles triangle, where $AB=BC.$\n\nHence, the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {4}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
